#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=8 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974088148'; [Fri Nov 06 15:08:08 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!Pairwise F_ST among 14 populations of the snow sheep (Ovis nivicola), Table S1 of Dotsev et al. (2026),
Ecology and Evolution 16:e74182, DOI 10.1002/ece3.74182 (CC BY), with the colours of the paper as display labels.
Figure 3 of the RazorNet paper: RazorNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 14 taxa and a 14 x 14 distance matrix.
The Razor Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 61 nodes and 83 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 34 nodes and 40 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

